 |\n| **Title** | [Watson Harmony] Spike in crashes \u2014 Azure Local Edge Observability (Cloud) in Public cloud |\n| **Spike Detected** | 2026-04-22 13:30 UTC |\n| **IcM Triggered** | 2026-04-26 00:00:15 UTC |\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause (Current Understanding)\nThis is a **Watson crash telemetry spike** in the \u0060Azure Local Edge Observability (Cloud)\u0060 service tree (ID: \u0060f34786ce-e806-490c-a554-53412253c5b0\u0060). No RCA has been authored yet \u2014 investigation is ongoing.\n\n#### Top Failure Buckets (by dump count)\n\n| Dumps | Exception | Component |\n|---|---|---|\n| **139** | \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException\u0060 (0x80070005) | \u0060TraceEvent.dll\u0060 \u2014 \u0060TraceEventSession..ctor\u0060 |\n| **113** | \u0060Win32Exception\u0060 (0x80004005) | \u0060ClusterApi.dll\u0060 \u2014 \u0060SafeClusterHandle.OpenClusterHandle\u0060 |\n| **59** | \u0060ArgumentException\u0060 (0x80070057) | \u0060UpdateService.Core.dll\u0060 \u2014 Unknown |\n| **36** | \u0060ConnectionFailureException\u0060 (0x80131500) | \u0060Http.Client.Remoting.dll\u0060 \u2014 Unknown |\n| **24** | \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException\u0060 (0x80070005) | \u0060UpdateService.Service.dll\u0060 \u2014 \u0060UnityConfig.RegisterCaching\u0060 |\n\n#### Faulting Processes\n| Process/Module | Dumps |\n|---|---|\n| \u0060microsoft.azurestack.updateservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060 | 381 |\n| \u0060agentlifecycleagenthost.dll\u0060 | 170 |\n| \u0060microsoft.diagnostics.tracing.traceevent.dll\u0060 | 146 |\n| \u0060microsoft.azurestack.common.infrastructure.http.client.remoting.dll\u0060 | 67 |\n| \u0060downloadservice.winsvchost.exe\u0060 | 36 |\n| \u0060edgecommonclient.dll\u0060 | 12 |\n| Region: **Japan East** | 56 |\n\n---\n\n### Analysis\n\n1. **Access denied creating ETW sessions** \u2014 The top bucket (\u0060TraceEventSession..ctor\u0060 \u2192 \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException\u0060) indicates the Update Service process lacks privileges to create ETW trace sessions. This is likely a permissions regression \u2014 possibly a change to service account privileges or a policy tightening.\n\n2. **Cluster API access failures** \u2014 \u0060SafeClusterHandle.OpenClusterHandle\u0060 failing with \u0060Win32Exception\u0060 suggests the process can\u0027t open the Windows Failover Cluster handle. This typically means the service account doesn\u0027t have cluster access, or the cluster service is not running/reachable on the target host.\n\n3. **Caching initialization failure** \u2014 \u0060UnityConfig.RegisterCaching\u0060 with \u0060UnauthorizedAccessException\u0060 suggests the service can\u0027t write to registry or protected paths during startup dependency injection setup.\n\n4. **Connectivity failures** \u2014 \u0060ConnectionFailureException\u0060 in the HTTP remoting layer may be a downstream consequence of the above startup failures, or independent networking issues.\n\n5. **Scope**: NonProd subscriptions only; Japan East is the highest-impacted region. No correlated Ev2 deployments were identified in the spike window.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Check service account privileges** \u2014 Verify the Update Service\u0027s service account still has: (a) the \u0060SeSystemtimePrivilege\u0060 / ETW session creation rights, (b) cluster API read permissions, (c) registry write access for the caching paths.\n\n2. **Review recent policy/GPO changes** around 2026-04-22 in Japan East that could have restricted service account permissions.\n\n3. **Check for recent OS updates** \u2014 Windows OS patches deployed to Japan East nodes around April 22 could have changed ETW session privilege behavior.\n\n4. **Investigate \u0060agentlifecycleagenthost.dll\u0060 crashes** (170 dumps) \u2014 This is the second highest and may represent a separate failure mode in the agent lifecycle subsystem.\n\n5. **Use Azure Watson Portal links** (from the IcM summary) to drill into each bucket, download crash dumps, and identify the exact call stack.\n\n6. **Acknowledge and assign** \u2014 The incident is currently only acknowledged. It should be assigned to a DRI for active investigation per the TSG guidelines in the IcM summary.\n\n---\n\n**Files saved to:** \u0060E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\\u0060\n\n[OUTPUT:incidentFolder] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\n[OUTPUT:summary.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\summary.md\n[OUTPUT:discussion.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\discussion.md\n[OUTPUT:rca.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\rca.md\n[OUTPUT:metadata.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\metadata.md\n[OUTPUT:ai_summary.md]","ai.success":true,"ai.model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","ai.durationMs":129657,"ai.inputTokens":481441,"ai.outputTokens":4178,"incidentFolder":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093","summary.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\summary.md","discussion.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\discussion.md","rca.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\rca.md","metadata.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\UpdateService\\784334093\\metadata.md"},"globalVariables":{"maxQueryScore":0,"body.timestamp":"2026-04-26T00:00:15.265Z","codeIssueFile":"","agentFolder":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 784334093,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-26T00:00:15.265Z\u0022\n}","repoMdFile":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki\\repos.md","body.incidentId":784334093,"rcaFile":"","metadataFile":"","body.serviceName":"","discussionFile":"","mitigationStepsFile":"","body.teamName":"","rootRepoFolder":"E:\\work","incidentId":0,"queryLoopCount":0,"applicableTsgFile":"","incidentFolder":"","etwEventsFile":"","summaryFile.md":"","issueListFile":""}}}
